course: dictionary
lesson: 2279
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. «You've cremated the toast!» is a joke: the word toast tells you the food was burned very badly.
explain: Cremate has a serious meaning too. When someone dies, their family may choose cremation, which means the body is burned until only ashes are left. Burial is the other choice, where the body is put in the ground. The word body and the word funeral are the clues that show this serious meaning.
explain: To check which meaning fits, put your meaning into the sentence and read it again. If «cremated the toast» means burned the toast, it makes sense. If a sentence talks about a funeral and memories, you know it is the serious meaning.
fact: Cremate is a verb: cremate, cremates, cremated, cremating.
fact: «Cremate» means to burn a body after death until only ashes are left.
fact: «Cremated remains» means the ashes left after a cremation.
fact: Many Hindus and many Christians choose cremation; Catholic and Orthodox Christians often prefer burial, and Hindus and Sikhs usually cremate.
fact: Informal, joking: «You've cremated the toast!» means you have burned the food very badly.
exercise: «You've cremated the toast!» What does cremated mean here? | Buried in the garden | Frozen solid | *Burned very badly | Eaten all in one go
exercise: «Many Hindus and many Christians choose cremation.» What is cremation? | Washing a body in water | *Burning a body until only ashes are left | A kind of cloth | Putting a body into the ground
exercise: In «At a Hindu funeral the body is usually cremated», which word tells you the word is about a person, not food? | Hindu | At | usually | *funeral
test: «Walt Disney was cremated after he died in 1966.» What does cremated mean? | Put in the ground | Kept frozen | Sung over | *Burned until only ashes are left
test: Which form of cremate is the past tense? | cremates | *cremated | cremate | cremating
exam: Is cremated serious or joking in «They share memories, sing or pray, and then the body is buried or cremated.»? | Joking, because buried is a joke | Joking, because sing is funny | Not a real word | *Serious, because it talks of the body, memories and prayers
